# Copy to `.env` and fill in real values. `.env` is gitignored.

# ----- Microsoft Entra ID (OIDC) — the identity source (#119) -----
#
# Direct MSAL auth-code flow (replaces Stack Auth). Provision the app
# registration + redirect URIs + delegated Graph scopes per
# `docs/deployment/entra-setup.md`, then fill these in. Server-side only —
# none are VITE_-prefixed, so they never reach the browser bundle.
AZURE_TENANT_ID=''          # tenant (directory) GUID
AZURE_CLIENT_ID=''          # app registration (client) id
AZURE_CLIENT_SECRET=''      # from the app's "Certificates & secrets"

# HMAC key that signs the auth cookies. Generate: `openssl rand -base64 32`.
AUTH_SESSION_SECRET=''

# Encrypts the per-user Microsoft token cache at rest (#110 — that cache holds
# refresh tokens). Generate: `openssl rand -base64 32`. When unset, the key is
# HKDF-derived from AUTH_SESSION_SECRET; set it explicitly in production so the
# two can rotate independently. Rotating it invalidates stored caches, which
# only means affected users sign in again.
# TOKEN_ENCRYPTION_KEY=''

# REQUIRED once any conversation has been saved. Encrypts stored user content
# and personal data at rest — conversation titles and the full context blob,
# session/user email + display name, routine input + label — with AES-256-GCM,
# so a pg_dump or a stolen volume yields ciphertext. Generate:
# `openssl rand -base64 32`.
#
# Deliberately its OWN variable, with no fallback: rotating AUTH_SESSION_SECRET
# logs everyone out and rotating TOKEN_ENCRYPTION_KEY makes users sign in again,
# but rotating this one makes every stored conversation unreadable unless it is
# re-encrypted first. Sharing key material would couple the cheap rotations to
# the expensive one.
#
# BACK IT UP SEPARATELY FROM THE DATABASE. It is not recoverable from the rows
# it protects: a restored dump without this key is ciphertext forever. Starting
# with encrypted rows present and no key is a deliberate hard boot failure.
DATA_ENCRYPTION_KEY=''

# Escape hatch for the delegated Graph scopes requested at sign-in (#110).
# Defaults to the full connector set (profile + mail + calendar + files); every
# scope must be consented under API permissions FIRST, or sign-in fails
# outright. Set a trimmed space/comma-separated list here to drop a problem
# scope without a code change. See docs/deployment/entra-setup.md.
# AZURE_GRAPH_SCOPES='User.Read email Mail.Read'

# IANA timezone Graph renders calendar times in (default: the server's own zone).
# Set when the app and its users don't share a timezone.
# GRAPH_TIMEZONE='Europe/Brussels'

# OIDC redirect / post-logout URIs. Defaults target dev (port 3444); the
# redirect MUST match a Redirect URI registered on the app (Web platform).
# AUTH_REDIRECT_URI='http://localhost:3444/api/auth/callback'
# AUTH_POST_LOGOUT_REDIRECT_URI='http://localhost:3444/auth/signin'

# ----- Legacy: Neon Auth (Stack Auth) — being removed by #119 -----
# Kept only for reference during the Entra cutover; no longer read by the app.
# VITE_STACK_PROJECT_ID=''
# VITE_STACK_PUBLISHABLE_CLIENT_KEY=''
# STACK_SECRET_SERVER_KEY=''

# Email allow-list for real auth (comma-separated; supports `*@domain.com`).
VITE_ALLOWED_EMAILS=''

# ----- LLM providers -----
# Anthropic is the only LLM provider: every BAML chain is Anthropic-only
# (see "BAML client routing" below), so this is the only key the app needs
# to answer a message.
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=''
# Optional, and NOT an LLM-routing key: the `openrouter` Data Stash embedding
# provider (EMBEDDINGS_PROVIDER=openrouter). Unused on the `local` default.
OPENROUTER_API_KEY=''

# Optional: Postgres connection (Neon). Defaults to local docker compose.
# DATABASE_URL=''

# ----- Dev auth bypass -----
#
# Default 'true' so `pnpm dev` works without a Stack Auth session — the app
# signs you in as the shared mock user `dev-bypass-user`. See
# `app/src/lib/auth/dev-bypass.ts` for the gate.
#
# This var is gated on `import.meta.env.DEV` and is structurally ignored in
# production builds — Vite replaces DEV with `false` at build time. If this
# var leaks into a prod build, the app warns at startup but does NOT honor it.
#
# How to enable real auth (test the Entra sign-in locally):
#   1. Fill in the AZURE_* + AUTH_SESSION_SECRET values above.
#   2. Set VITE_DEV_BYPASS_AUTH='false' below.
#   3. `pnpm dev`, open /auth/signin, click "Sign in with Microsoft", and use
#      an account whose email is listed in VITE_ALLOWED_EMAILS above.
VITE_DEV_BYPASS_AUTH='true'

# ----- BAML client routing -----
#
# Anthropic is the only provider. Every BAML call (Router / LoopController /
# ActorController / Critic / Synthesize / ResultDescribe /
# GenerateConversationTitle / ReferenceSelector) is declared with an
# Anthropic chain in `baml_src/anthropic-only.baml`, so ANTHROPIC_API_KEY
# above is the only provider key the app needs. There is no routing env var:
# the mixed Groq / OpenRouter / OpenAI chains and USE_MIXED_CHAINS were
# removed 2026-08-24 (docs/adr/0001-anthropic-only-default-chains.md).
# To re-point a role, edit `app/src/lib/harness-patterns/clients.server.ts`.

# ----- Data Stash: direct Redis (ingest/search speedup) -----
#
# The Data Stash vector pipeline (chunk → embed → index → KNN) normally goes
# through the MCP gateway, whose serial stdio pipe (~1.6s/call) makes ingest
# slow (~200s for a large doc). Set to '1' to route the Data Stash APP path
# through a direct ioredis connection instead (sub-millisecond per call, ingest
# in < 1s). Only affects the Data Stash — agentic MCP tool use still goes
# through the gateway. Hits the SAME redis-stack the gateway writes, so the
# vector schema is compatible. Requires redis-stack reachable (see below) and,
# on arm64 colima, the linux/amd64 override (docs/DATA_STASH.md).
# STASH_DIRECT_REDIS='1'
#
# Connection for the direct client (defaults shown; dev redis is auth-less).
# REDIS_HOST_DIRECT='localhost'   # falls back to REDIS_HOST, then 'localhost'
# REDIS_PORT='6379'
# REDIS_PWD=''                    # falls back to REDIS_PASSWORD
# REDIS_SSL='false'               # 'true' to connect over TLS

# ----- Data Stash: document → markdown conversion -----
#
# By default only text-like uploads (md, txt, csv, json, html, …) are ingested
# for search; binary office/PDF files are stored but not searchable. Set to '1'
# to convert binary uploads (docx, odt, pptx, pdf) to markdown via the
# `doc-convert` sidecar (see docker-compose.yaml) so they get chunked/embedded
# and become searchable + viewable. The original bytes are kept for download.
# Requires the sidecar running; if it's unreachable the upload still succeeds
# and the doc is marked ingest-failed (search just won't include it).
# STASH_CONVERT_DOCS='1'
#
# Base URL of the conversion sidecar (default shown). Override when the app runs
# inside the compose network (then use http://doc-convert:8000).
# DOC_CONVERT_URL='http://localhost:8000'
# DOC_CONVERT_TIMEOUT_MS='120000'  # per-file conversion timeout
